   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Adjectives agree",
     "texto": [
      "Adjectives change according to the noun they accompany: **casa grande** (big house), **prédio grande** (big block of flats), **casas grandes** (big houses).",
      "In Portuguese the adjective almost always goes **after** the noun: **uma casa bonita** (a pretty house). Only some go before, such as **bom** (good) and **mau** (bad): **um bom bairro** (a good neighbourhood)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The plural of adjectives",
     "texto": [
      "Those ending in **-o** or **-a** form the plural with **-s**: **bonito/bonitos**, **bonita/bonitas**. Those ending in **-e** also add **-s**: **grande/grandes**.",
      "Several adjectives ending in **-l** change their ending: **-al → -ais** (**normal/normais**), **-el → -éis** (**cruel/cruéis**) and **-il átono → -eis** (**fácil/fáceis**). For **-il tónico** it is usually **-is** (**juvenil/juvenis**). **Azul/azuis** is another frequent form. Learn the most common examples; the patterns depend on the ending and on the stress."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
